Subject: [PATCH] drm/exynos: hdmi: support small HDMI screens on Exynos 5420/5422

Mainline only knows 18 HDMI PHY settings for the Exynos 5420 family and
requires the mode's pixel clock to match one of them exactly. Small HDMI
screens (typically 800x480 at about 30-34 MHz) never do, so their only
mode is rejected and the screen stays dark.

Use the table from Hardkernel's Odroid XU4 kernel, and pick the
nearest PHY clock within 2% instead of requiring an exact match. Hardkernel's
196.9 MHz entry is left out, as its values do not fit in bytes.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos_hdmi.c	2026-10-13 19:37:13.731191863 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos_hdmi.c	2026-10-13 19:39:52.174005661 +0200
@@ -368,6 +368,12 @@
 	},
 };
 
+/*
+ * Taken from Hardkernel's kernel for the Odroid XU4 (odroid-6.6.y): besides the
+ * mainline entries it covers clocks used by small HDMI screens (e.g. 800x480 at
+ * 31.49, 32 or 33.9 MHz), which mainline rejects, leaving such screens dark.
+ * Hardkernel's 196.9 MHz entry is left out: its values do not fit in bytes.
+ */
